this is a hand-built text approximation of a Chromium disk-cache
"data_2" index file, kept as plain text on purpose so the fixture stays
diffable and reviewable. real data_2 files are binary (Chromium block-file
format); the plugin's urlPattern only ever runs against text the Rust host
has already extracted from it, so a text sample is sufficient to prove
urlPattern matches a real request URL. no real cache bytes, no real authkey.
note: urlPattern's tail is `[^"]+` (matches until the next literal quote
character), so this fixture deliberately terminates the URL with a `"` —
without one, the pattern would greedily swallow everything to end of file.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
\x00\x00\x00\x01BLK1garbage-block-header-bytes-not-real-cache-format\x00
"https://public-operation-nap.mihoyo.com/common/gacha_record/api/getGachaLog?authkey_ver=1&sign_type=2&auth_appid=webview_gacha&init_log_gacha_base_type=1&lang=zh-cn&device_type=pc&game_biz=nap_cn&authkey=FAKE_AUTHKEY_FOR_FIXTURE_ONLY&game_version=CNRELWin1.0.0&plat_type=pc&region=prod_gf_cn&os_system=Windows%2010&device_model=FIXTURE-PC&page=1&size=20&real_gacha_type=2&end_id=0"
\x00\x00tail-garbage-after-the-cached-entry\x00\x00
